.PP
.SH "Motivation"
.PP
The \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP module is provided to allow users to perform passive advection and advection of a single non-wetting phase in two-phase flow simulations\&. It represents the fastest but CFL dependent transport scheme for arbitrary FE meshes including different FE types and mixes of volume and surface elements\&. 
.br

.PP
The scheme is also very tolerant in that no specific boundary conditions need to be applied\&. The value of the advected variable at inflow boundaries is not modified and governs what gets transported into the model domain\&. 
.br
.SH "Design Intent"
.PP
The scheme has been designed to capitalize on the new generic polytype CVFE technology that is part of CSMP\&. 
.br
.SH "Applicability"
.PP
Use the scheme if the transport velocity field is rapidly changing or invalidated by the transport itself\&. In this case the scheme is faster that the implicit scheme embodied in the FiniteVolumeTransport module which starts to pay off at about CFL=20 or greater\&. 
.br

.PP
Do not use this scheme when the CFL condition based transport increment leads global advection steps that are smaller than about 1/1,000 of the model length in the direction of the flow\&. In this case the computations would be prohibitively slow\&.
.SH "Structure"
.PP
The user will only interact with the \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP module, but the FiniteVolumeAlgorithm is used to manage the accumulation and output of the solution in each transport step, and the FiniteVolumeProcessor class facilitates the generation of the finite-volume stencils from each finite element, so that the accumulation can proceed on an element by element basis and no FV mesh needs to be stored\&.
.SH "Collaboration"
.PP
The scheme collaborates with the finite elements of the current model\&.
.SH "Consequences"
.PP
This implementation of the scheme cannot be restricted to Regions, but always needs to be applied to the entire model, i\&.e\&. \fBModel\fP\&. 
.br

.PP
Currently it also only works for 3D models\&. Surface computations can still be done if the mesh consists entirely of surface elements in 3D space\&. 
.SH "Constructor & Destructor Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class STP> \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP< dim, STP >::TwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport (const char * group_name, \fBModel\fP< dim > & sg, const char * porosity = \fR'porosity'\fP, const char * viscosity_n = \fR'viscosity carbonic phase'\fP, const char * viscosity_w = \fR'viscosity aqueous phase'\fP, const char * density_n = \fR'density carbonic phase'\fP, const char * density_w = \fR'density aqueous phase'\fP, const char * phase1_to_update = \fR'saturation aqueous phase'\fP, const char * phase2_to_advect = \fR'saturation carbonic phase'\fP, const char * transp_velocity = \fR'velocity'\fP, const char * nodal_source = \fR'nodal fluid volume source'\fP, bool with_capillary_spreading = \fRfalse\fP, bool with_gravitational_forces = \fRfalse\fP, const char * reference_variable_to_reference_variable_to_no_flow_bc = \fR'fluid pressure'\fP, bool nonlinear_scheme = \fRfalse\fP)"

.PP
First-order two-phase flow constructor, no capillary spreading, wetting phase=phase1\&. Constructor for the modelling of two-phase slightly compressible flow with fluid density and viscosity variations\&. The properties fluid density and viscosity are expected to be node variables and are interpolated to the FV facet integration points to carry out the computations\&. The transport scheme is setup for the non-wetting phase\&. The onus is on the user to update the second phase saturations after each advection step, i\&.e\&., calculate sw=1-sn\&. 
.br

.PP
The \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP can be constructed for first- and second order calculations\&. 
.br

.PP
Diffusion is only taken into account if second-order is chosen, because the first-order scheme already is so diffusive that adding an extra diffusion term makes little sense\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP gains access via reference to the model to which it is applied to\&. The user needs to specify the piecewise constant element variables porosity, diffusivity and transport velocity\&. These must be defined in the CSP_variables\&.txt file\&. The variables fluid density and viscosity of the wetting and non-wetting phases must be nodal variables as well\&. They are interpolated to the facet and sector integration points using the finite element basis functions\&. 
.br

.PP
The transported variable must be nodal since this explicit transport scheme is based on node-centered finite volumes\&. 
.br
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
This constructor creates a minor storage array for repetitively used variables like the finite (pore) volumes, the flux balance for each FV cell and a \fBvector<double>\fP of FV_parameters called FV_stencil_data that holds the FV sector volumes, facet areas and facet normal fluxes which are always updated before the first advection step, when the CFL criterion is computed\&. This \fBvector<double>\fP will become redundant when the generic FV scheme has been optimized for speed\&. 
.br
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Use \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP as constructed with this particular constructor for two-phase flow in a rapidly evolving flow field that necessitates frequent updates of the velocity fields\&. 
.br

.PP
For a weak coupling between phase saturations and total mobility, use the implicit transport module FiniteVolumeTransport\&. 
.br
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The memory that is consumed during the construction process is reported\&.

.PP
Constructor for first-order scheme\&. 
.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class STP> \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP< dim, STP >::TwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport (const char * group_name, \fBModel\fP< dim > & sg, const char * porosity, const char * diffusivity, const char * viscosity_n, const char * viscosity_w, const char * density_n, const char * density_w, const char * phase1_to_update, const char * phase2_to_advect, const char * transp_velocity, const char * nodal_source, bool with_capillary_spreading = \fRfalse\fP, bool with_gravitational_forces = \fRfalse\fP, const char * reference_variable_to_no_flow_bc = \fR'fluid pressure'\fP, bool nonlinear_scheme = \fRfalse\fP)"

.PP
First-order two-phase flow constructor, with capillary spreading modelled as non-linear diffusion\&. Constructor for the modelling of two-phase slightly compressible flow with fluid density and viscosity variations\&. The properties fluid density and viscosity are expected to be node variables and are interpolated to the FV facet integration points to carry out the computations\&. The transport scheme is setup for the non-wetting phase\&. The onus is on the user to update the second phase saturations after each advection step, i\&.e\&., calculate sw=1-sn\&.

.PP
The \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP can be constructed for first- and second order calculations\&.

.PP
Diffusion is only taken into account if second-order is chosen, because the first-order scheme already is so diffusive that adding an extra diffusion term makes little sense\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP gains access via reference to the model to which it is applied to\&. The user needs to specify the piecewise constant element variables porosity, diffusivity and transport velocity\&. These must be defined in the CSP_variables\&.txt file\&. The variables fluid density and viscosity of the wetting and non-wetting phases must be nodal variables as well\&. They are interpolated to the facet and sector integration points using the finite element basis functions\&.

.PP
The transported variable must be nodal since this explicit transport scheme is based on node-centered finite volumes\&.
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
This constructor creates a minor storage array for repetitively used variables like the finite (pore) volumes, the flux balance for each FV cell and a \fBvector<double>\fP of FV_parameters called FV_stencil_data that holds the FV sector volumes, facet areas and facet normal fluxes which are always updated before the first advection step, when the CFL criterion is computed\&. This \fBvector<double>\fP will become redundant when the generic FV scheme has been optimized for speed\&.
.SH "Application Examples"
.PP
Use \fBTwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP as constructed with this particular constructor for two-phase flow in a rapidly evolving flow field that necessitates frequent updates of the velocity fields\&.

.PP
For a weak coupling between phase saturations and total mobility, use the implicit transport module FiniteVolumeTransport\&.
.SH "Messages"
.PP
The memory that is consumed during the construction process is reported\&. 
