.SS "template<uint32_t dim, template< uint32_t > class STP> double \fBcsmp::TwoPhaseImplicitNodeCenteredFVTransport\fP< dim, STP >::TransportPhase (\fBTwoPhaseModel\fP< dim > & relperm, double time_interval)\fR [virtual]\fP"

.PP
transport of a non-wetting phase in 2-phase flow The method is the equivalent to \fBAdvectVariable()\fP for 2-phase flow\&. Thus, it advects the transport variable for the user-specified time interval and writes the results back to the current \fBModel\fP object\&. 
.br
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
The method takes a reference to the \fBModel\fP object which contains the transport variable field that shall be advected\&. The relative permeabilities and other 2-phase properties are obtained via the supplied 'AdvectionDiffusionTwoPhaseModel'\&. The onus is on the user to make sure that the necessary variables are defined and initialized\&. The third method argument is the time interval over which the transport variable shall be advected\&. 
.br

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
The advected variable field is written back into the supplied \fBModel\fP\&. The method returns the CFL condition that it determined before the onset of the advection\&.
.RE
.PP
.SH "Implementation"
.PP
The CFL_FACTOR is a multiplier that represents the maximum factor by which the diameter of the idealized spherical FV can be multiplied while the transport scheme is stable\&. 
.PP
Reimplemented from \fBcsmp::NodeCenteredFiniteVolumeTransport< dim >\fP\&.

